WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:03.221
Expand Advanced Automation and open Workflows.

00:00:03.541 --> 00:00:06.699
Read the description and select the service actually available.

00:00:07.083 --> 00:00:12.032
Integrated Foundation Central, standalone F C A and classic Foundation V M

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.436
use different contracts.

00:00:13.645 --> 00:00:17.698
Import or complete the matching form and review its generated configuration.

00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:21.751
Do not assume that a similarly named action has the same credentials or

00:00:21.837 --> 00:00:23.074
execution semantics.

00:00:23.415 --> 00:00:26.024
Open Scripts for a specific allowlisted action.

00:00:26.328 --> 00:00:30.296
Use its parameter wizard and installed schema, then review the generated

00:00:30.381 --> 00:00:31.021
input.

00:00:31.277 --> 00:00:34.712
A script sequence and a workflow are different launch modes.

00:00:35.032 --> 00:00:39.178
Supply the required saved file and inspect verification after execution.

00:00:39.619 --> 00:00:44.013
Set Prism Login Title for P E is now available as a focused script or

00:00:44.056 --> 00:00:47.635
pipeline action, with title-only Configure Cluster support.

00:00:48.057 --> 00:00:51.726
Review the exact title and cluster, select the correct vault credential

00:00:51.939 --> 00:00:54.423
reference and retain certificate verification.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:59.008
The action compares the existing setting, applies a change only when needed,

00:00:59.221 --> 00:01:02.592
and requires a fresh readback to verify the requested title.

00:01:03.018 --> 00:01:07.882
Legacy U I A P I compatibility still needs validation against the target A O

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:08.724
S version.

00:01:09.096 --> 00:01:13.747
A saved title or subprocess success alone does not prove the target displays

00:01:13.832 --> 00:01:14.117
it.

00:01:14.515 --> 00:01:18.184
For local P E users choose Create Local Users for P E.

00:01:18.355 --> 00:01:21.880
Each requested username needs its own matching credential reference.

00:01:22.163 --> 00:01:26.707
Select the intended role set explicitly and respect the installed schema.

00:01:27.027 --> 00:01:28.918
Run Dry Run before submission.

00:01:29.273 --> 00:01:33.753
After creation, independently confirm that each account is enabled and has

00:01:33.796 --> 00:01:37.707
both Cluster Admin and User Admin when those are the approved roles.

00:01:38.276 --> 00:01:42.231
Inspect the stage and safe category when local user creation fails.

00:01:42.603 --> 00:01:47.445
Credential resolution, certificate trust, identity mismatch, network access,

00:01:47.808 --> 00:01:52.096
creation, role assignment and verification are separate failure points.

00:01:52.416 --> 00:01:55.348
Check whether any accounts or roles were already created.

00:01:55.719 --> 00:01:59.644
Correct the actual cause and rerun only through the supported process.

00:02:00.028 --> 00:02:04.278
Do not paste passwords or raw authentication headers into a support request.

00:02:04.841 --> 00:02:09.151
The C V M and Dell i D R A C rotation workflow has a separate support

00:02:09.364 --> 00:02:11.305
boundary and exact confirmations.

00:02:11.668 --> 00:02:16.404
Verify each C V M host-key fingerprint independently, establish the required

00:02:16.532 --> 00:02:19.223
access and keep an out-of-band recovery path.

00:02:19.568 --> 00:02:23.280
Review any manual follow-up, including host I P M I credential

00:02:23.493 --> 00:02:24.368
synchronization.

00:02:24.688 --> 00:02:28.955
A dry run or approval does not prove that live rotation is validated for

00:02:28.997 --> 00:02:30.435
your firmware and release.
